# sky130-modexp #154: the Curator heartbeat-idempotency fix. Root-caused live
# on this repo's issue #12, which collected 44 `curator:operator-premise-
# recheck` comments in a month (27 of 43 gaps under the 24h window, minimum 23
# minutes). `dep-recheck-fingerprint.sh decide` was NOT wrong -- the prior
# marker handed to it was. 19 of the 22 post-2026-09-11 spam comments name the
# same predecessor, "2026-09-10 12:46 UTC", which is exactly that thread's 30th
# comment: page one of `GET /issues/{n}/comments` at its default per_page=30.
#
# The fix is two things, both of which live in the installed copies because the
# arithmetic they feed is upstream Rust (`loom-daemon/src/dep_recheck/`):
#   1. a pagination-safe, fail-closed prior-marker reader, and
#   2. a confirm-under-claim re-decide in curator.md's two idempotency paths,
#      so two concurrent passes cannot both conclude "reportable".
# Upstream PR: TBD (see 2am#869) -- the reader belongs in defaults/scripts/ and
# the prompt change in defaults/commands/loom/curator.md.

# scripts/dep-recheck-prior-marker.sh: the new reader (no upstream counterpart
#   yet, so an unpinned resync would ORPHAN/remove it, not merely revert it).
scripts/dep-recheck-prior-marker.sh

# scripts/tests/test-dep-recheck-prior-marker.sh: the hermetic regression suite
#   (replays #12's page-boundary shape; wired into this repo's own CI).
# scripts/tests/test-dep-recheck-heartbeat-race.sh: the two-concurrent-passes
#   scenario, driving the real `decide` (needs a built loom-daemon).
scripts/tests/test-dep-recheck-prior-marker.sh
scripts/tests/test-dep-recheck-heartbeat-race.sh

